    },
    {
      "id": "s2",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "hue_womb",
      "narration": "They form before birth, roughly between weeks ten and sixteen of pregnancy.",
      "on_screen_text": "Before you're born",
      "highlight_words": [
        "born"
      ],
      "sfx": "riser",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s3",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "hue_ridges",
      "narration": "The skin on your fingertips folds into ridges and grooves, like tiny waves.",
      "on_screen_text": "Ridges and grooves",
      "highlight_words": [
        "Ridges"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s4",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "hue_patterns",
      "narration": "Those ridges form three basic patterns: arches, loops and whorls.",
      "on_screen_text": "Arches, loops, whorls",
      "highlight_words": [
        "whorls"
      ],
      "sfx": "pop",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s5",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "hue_unique",
      "narration": "But the details, like where each line ends or splits, are unique to each person.",
      "on_screen_text": "Unique details",
      "highlight_words": [
        "Unique"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s6",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "hue_twins",
      "narration": "Not even identical twins have the same fingerprints.",
      "on_screen_text": "Not even twins",
      "highlight_words": [
        "twins"
      ],
      "sfx": "ding",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s7",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "hue_touch",
      "narration": "And they help you feel: when you slide a finger, the ridges vibrate and your brain picks up textures better.",
      "on_screen_text": "Feeling textures",
      "highlight_words": [
        "textures"
      ],
      "sfx": "whoosh",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s8",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "hue_police",
      "narration": "That's why police have used them to identify people for over a hundred years.",
      "on_screen_text": "Identifying for 100+ years",
      "highlight_words": [
        "100+"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
