  "description": "Fingerprints form before birth, roughly between weeks 10 and 16 of pregnancy. The skin folds into ridges that make arches, loops or whorls, and their details are unique, even between identical twins. They help sense texture because they vibrate as a finger slides, they've been used to identify people for over a century, and koalas have fingerprints very similar to ours. Original 3D animation.",
